```
n. Delims: replace concatenation with verb + path f-string composition
    [ ] 'content/backend/core/core/entities.py': Consolidate fileset delims into a verb-driven helper
        - Introduce a verb enum (create, update, delete, file, file_meta) with open/close/self-closing methods
        - Collapse CREATE/UPDATE/READ_FILESET_UL, *_BL, DELETE_FILESET_UL, FILE_META_UL, FILE_META_CLOSE, FILESET_OPEN_END_TAG(_BR) into verb methods
        - Keep FILELIST and PROMPT delims as-is (single-char, no path)
    [ ] 'content/backend/render_pipeline/render_service.py': Align multi-doc rendering to the same verb source
        - `_res_multi_doc` currently hand-assembles `<name>…</name>` bookends via Delims concatenation
        - Refactor to derive open/close from the shared verb helper so fileset and filelist rendering share one composition path
    [ ] 'content/backend/asset_ingestion/ingestion_parser.py': Derive regex patterns from verb definitions
        - `_open_re` and `_close_re` currently embed escaped Delims strings inline
        - Refactor to build the pattern from the verb set so adding a verb updates the parser automatically
    [ ] 'content/a_lib/shared-assets/prompt-fragments/output-instructions/code-generation.output-template': Consider composing the example block at render time
        - Template currently mirrors parser tags by hand
        - If verbs are the source of truth, the example section could be generated from the verb set rather than maintained as a static file
        - Token substitution layer (§fsoet§ etc.) becomes optional if display strings are emitted directly
```

